#! python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
VehicleTurn_VD_v12.py
Rhino 8 / CPython / RhinoCommon + Eto

Vejdirektoratet template-based vehicle-turn tool.

This version intentionally does NOT simulate steering for standard turns.  The curve library
is embedded from the uploaded Korekurver QGIS v1.2 dataset, which was converted from the
Vejdirektoratet DWG turning-curve files and tagged by vehicle, driving mode and direction.
The QGIS plugin documentation states its GIS conversion may differ from the source CAD by
up to about 3 cm.  Keeping the original Vejdirektoratet DWGs as a future exact source is
therefore worthwhile, but this version should already track the published geometry closely.

Workflow
1. Pick an incoming straight road centreline on the approach side.
2. Pick an outgoing straight road centreline on the departure side.
3. VehicleTurn detects left/right and the included angle, then selects the nearest published
   Vejdirektoratet gon curve for the chosen vehicle/mode.
4. In single-lane mode the template straight-path centre lies on the selected centrelines.
   In two-way/right-hand mode it is placed on nominal lane centres (road width / 4 right of CL).
5. Road-fit checks compare the published design-envelope lines against the entered road width,
   with the entered clearance added as a design margin.
6. Create outputs ordinary Rhino curves on the CURRENT layer. No custom Rhino objects.

Notes
- Standard Vej template geometry is plan geometry. Sloped 3D input lines are accepted; output
  Z is blended between the two road grades so straight tails follow their respective grades.
- 200 gon / 180-degree U-turn templates need a separate one-road + turn-side placement workflow
  and are intentionally not exposed in this corner/junction command yet.
"""

